            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous rupture of pheochromocytoma: computed tomography-pathologic features and correlation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>230-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spontaneous rupture is a rare complication of pheochromocytoma. Its preoperative diagnosis is of great importance in determining treatment and prognosis. We describe computed tomography pathologic findings and correlate their features in a case with ruptured pheochromocytoma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
